# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file, patches or ignores known vulnerabilities.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-JOI-19778379:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-90771 (prototype pollution in joi). The fixed releases
          (joi 18.2.9 and 17.13.8, both published 2026-09-11) fall inside the
          7-day supply-chain cooldown enforced by min-release-age=7 in .npmrc,
          so `npm ci` rejects them with ETARGET. No joi version currently
          satisfies both the advisory and the cooldown.

          Exposure here is nil: the vulnerable code path is reached only via
          attacker-controlled input to joi's .messages() API, which this
          service never calls. All schemas under src/api/schemas use default
          messages.

          Remove this ignore and bump joi to 18.2.9 once the cooldown window
          clears on 2026-09-18.
        expires: 2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-SPRINTFJS-20532016:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          No fixed version exists for sprintf-js (Snyk advisory: "There is no fixed
          version"). Pulled in transitively via global-agent@3.0.0 > roarr@2.15.4 >
          sprintf-js@1.1.3, used only to format global-agent's own internal debug
          logging; no attacker-controlled format string reaches it in this service.
          global-agent 4.x (up to and including 4.1.3, the latest release) breaks
          outbound HTTPS-through-proxy TLS hostname validation
          (ERR_TLS_CERT_ALTNAME_INVALID), so 3.0.0 is pinned until that regression
          is fixed upstream. Re-review when either package publishes a fix.
        expires: 2026-12-17T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-HAPICONTENT-21691242:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          ReDoS in @hapi/content@6.0.2, pulled in via @hapi/hapi > @hapi/subtext and
          pinned by the @hapi/content override in package.json. The fixed release,
          6.0.3 (published 2026-10-21T16:25Z), falls inside the 7-day supply-chain
          cooldown enforced by min-release-age=7 in .npmrc, so `npm install` rejects
          it with ETARGET until 2026-10-28T16:25Z.

          @hapi/content parses request Content-Type and Content-Disposition headers,
          which clients control, so exposure is not nil; the ignore is kept short.

          Remove this ignore and change the override to 6.0.3 once the cooldown
          window clears.
        expires: 2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z
patch: {}
